{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringHeckeCommensurability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringHeckeCommensurability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.fricke_conj_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.fricke_conj_T","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L90-L96","doc":"(L1c) `W₂ T W₂ = -2 · [[1,0],[-2,1]]`: conjugating the integral translation by the\nFricke involution gives, projectively, the lower generator of `Γ₀(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.conj_sHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.conj_sHecke","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L81-L88","doc":"(L1b) `D S D⁻¹ = √2⁻¹ · W₂`: `S` becomes the Fricke involution projectively. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.conj_uHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.conj_uHecke","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L75-L79","doc":"(L1a) `D U D⁻¹ = T`: the Hecke translation by `√2` becomes translation by `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.dInv_mul_d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.dInv_mul_d","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L70-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.sqrt2_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.sqrt2_ne","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.fricke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.fricke","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L65-L66","doc":"Fricke involution `W₂ : z ↦ -1/(2z)`, as the integral matrix `[[0,-1],[2,0]]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.sHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.sHecke","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L62-L63","doc":"Hecke inversion `S : z ↦ -1/z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.uHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.uHecke","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Hecke translation `U : z ↦ z + √2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.dInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.dInv","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`D⁻¹ = diag(1, 1/√2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.dMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.dMat","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L53-L54","doc":"`D = diag(1, √2)`, the Möbius map `z ↦ z/√2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.tl_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.tl_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L41-L47","doc":"The image of `σ₀σ₁` is not `±1`, so the core is a nontrivial element of\n`SL(2,ℤ)` whose image in `PSL(2,ℤ)` is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.gammaGamma_core_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.gammaGamma_core_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L34-L39","doc":"(L2) The γγ core `(σ₀σ₁)³` maps to `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.lGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.lGen","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L31-L32","doc":"Image of `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringHecke.tGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringHecke.tGen","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringHeckeCommensurability.lean#L28-L29","doc":"Image of `σ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}